      {
        "h_title": "What’s the weather like on Koh Samui in August?",
        "main_title": "We send REALLY USEFUL emails",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The big question: will it rain in August? It very well might – but you’re going to choose not to care. Why? Don’t fixate on the weather (something you can’t control) – Koh Samui is gorgeous always, as are its drinks, food and people.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "How much does it rain on Koh Samui in August?",
        "main_title": "We send REALLY USEFUL emails",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Always expect rain in the tropics, but rest assured it never lasts very long. Plan some Koh Samui rainy day activities, just in case. As with Koh Samui in July, afternoon showers are pretty common in August. Here's an example:",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "4:12pm – storm comes out of nowhere",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Why should you disregard the high probability of storms like this? Almost everywhere has plastic roll-down screens. You just keep eating/reading/drinking/enjoying your Thai massage. Then the storm finishes, and you carry on. When the rain arrives you can almost always stay exactly where you are – enjoying the exact same hilarious company, cold beer and amazing Thai food.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "3:55pm – perfect sunshine",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "4:17pm - storm's here!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "How hot is it on Koh Samui in August?",
        "main_title": "We send REALLY USEFUL emails",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 4,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Expect an average daily high of 32°C (89.6°F) – right about perfect. When it’s sunny, it’s sunny with big, blue skies like you’ve never seen. It can be humid at this time of year – definitely two-showers-a-day territory.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
